OTC Fund Prototype

Blockchain-based OTC Fund Simulation (Local Anvil + Solidity + API + Web UI)

This repository contains a full-stack prototype of a blockchain-based OTC fund platform.
It simulates fund subscription, redemption, NAV posting, and audit export using:

Solidity smart contracts (FundToken + NAVRegistry)

Local Ethereum network (Anvil, Foundry toolchain)

Node.js API middleware

Next.js web UI with role-based portals

All transactions are simulated locally and do not involve real assets.

1. System Architecture (High-Level)
┌────────────┐        ┌──────────────┐        ┌────────────┐
│  Web UI    │ ─────▶ │  API Server  │ ─────▶ │  Contracts │
│ (Next.js)  │        │ (Node/TS)    │        │ (Solidity) │
└────────────┘        └──────────────┘        └────────────┘
                                                    │
                                                    ▼
                                                ┌────────┐
                                                │ Anvil  │
                                                │  EVM   │
                                                └────────┘

2. Prerequisites

Ensure the following are installed:

Node.js ≥ 18

pnpm (npm install -g pnpm)

Foundry (Forge, Anvil)

Install Foundry:

curl -L https://foundry.paradigm.xyz | bash
foundryup


Verify:

forge --version
anvil --version

3. Repository Structure
otc-prototype/
├── apps/
│   ├── api/          # Backend API (Node.js + TypeScript)
│   └── web/          # Frontend UI (Next.js)
├── contracts/        # Solidity smart contracts (Foundry)
├── README.md

4. Step-by-Step: Running the Full System

You will need four terminals.

Terminal 1 — Start Local Blockchain (Anvil)
anvil


Expected output:

Chain ID: 31337

RPC: http://127.0.0.1:8545

10 pre-funded test accounts

⚠️ Leave this running

Terminal 2 — Deploy Smart Contracts
cd contracts
forge build
forge test -vv


Deploy contracts:

forge script script/Deploy.s.sol:Deploy \
  --rpc-url http://127.0.0.1:8545 \
  --broadcast \
  --private-key 0xac0974bec39a17e36ba4a6b4d238ff944bacb478cbed5efcae784d7bf4f2ff80


Expected output:

FundToken:    0x...
NAVRegistry:  0x...
ONCHAIN EXECUTION COMPLETE & SUCCESSFUL.


These addresses are required by the API.

Terminal 3 — Start Backend API
cd apps/api
pnpm install
pnpm dev


API runs on:

http://localhost:3001

Health Check
curl http://localhost:3001/health

Terminal 4 — Start Web UI
cd apps/web
pnpm install
pnpm dev


Open browser:

http://localhost:3000

5. Available Web Portals
Home

Entry point

Navigation to all roles

Investor Portal

View token balance

Subscribe (mint fund tokens)

Redeem (burn fund tokens)

View risk status

Manager Console

Post NAV on-chain

View latest NAV

Simulates fund administrator actions

Auditor View

Export CSV of:

NAV postings

Subscriptions

Redemptions

Demonstrates immutable audit trail

6. API Endpoints (Key)
Health
GET /health

Risk Status
GET /risk

Token Balance
GET /token/balance/:address

Subscribe (Mint)
POST /token/subscribe
{
  "amount": "1000000000000000000"
}

Redeem (Burn)
POST /token/redeem
{
  "amount": "1000000000000000000"
}

Post NAV (Manager)
POST /nav/post
{
  "nav": "123456789",
  "asOf": 1710000000
}

Latest NAV
GET /nav/latest

Audit Export
GET /audit/export


Returns CSV.

7. Simulation Notes (Important)

All ETH is test ETH

All transactions are local-only

No real KYC, money, or external oracle is used

NAV values are manually supplied

The system demonstrates architecture and control flow, not production deployment

8. Common Troubleshooting
forge: command not found
export PATH="$HOME/.foundry/bin:$PATH"

API fails with BigInt error

The API serializes on-chain numeric fields as strings to avoid "Do not know how to serialize a BigInt".

Web UI does not update

Ensure API is running

Refresh page

Check browser console

9. Resetting the System

To reset all state:

Stop Anvil

Restart Anvil

Redeploy contracts

Restart API + Web